Subject: [PATCH 1/2] U14: study primitives Sheet, Stepper and PageHead; /study
 opens on PageHead

Three primitives the next units build on (MASTER-PLAN 8.1, 8.2):

- Sheet (components/study/Sheet.tsx): a bottom sheet on phones and a panel
  at the right edge from 1024px, on the Radix dialog already installed.
  Focus is trapped while open, Escape and Close close it, the page behind
  is hidden from assistive technology and held still, focus lands on the
  panel on open and returns to whatever opened it, with or without a
  Radix trigger. First use: VerseRef (U16).
- Stepper (components/study/Stepper.tsx): one step per screen, Back and
  Next in a bar that stays at the bottom in thumb reach, the position
  said plainly ("2 of 5"), focus on the new step's heading after a move,
  a finishing action on the last step, controlled or self-contained.
  First use: table mode (U17).
- PageHead (components/editorial/PageHead.tsx): eyebrow, the page's one
  H1, one line, optional actions, left-aligned on cream with a hairline.

Styles under .st- and .pg- in index.css, tokens only; one new token,
--scrim, for the dimmed page behind a sheet. Testing-library tests cover
keyboard and ARIA for all three.

One in, one out: /study now opens on PageHead instead of the charcoal
prose hero (the hero's second sentence is dropped; the Church history
group already says it), and the Study Bible heading steps down to sit
under the H1. On a 390px phone the "Open the Study Bible" button moves
from just below the first screen (857px) onto it (639px).

